<title>UK: UK's Clarke puts 3p/litre on gasoline, diesel.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke puts 3p/litre on gasoline, diesel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said Britain would increase tax on all petrol and diesel fuels by three pence per litre effective from 1800 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Clarke said he was sticking to his commitment to raise road fuel duties by an average of at least five percent each year in real terms.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
